[10890]="700589ED\n1\tSpeak with Óli\t\n2\tDefeat Azbauz and Maugrush\030Defeat Shatarkha\tSecure the eastern and western gate controls\n3\tDefeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk\tDefeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk and secure the Gate of Winds\n",
[10891]="7005D3F9\n1\tTalk to Penfold\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Shakalush, the Stair Battle, tiers 1-5 raid deeds.\n",
[10892]="70053E75\n1\tDefeat merrevail and mervyl\tMerrevail and mervyl can be found at Shakam Moz in Rath Dúath. You should defeat winged folk at Shakam Moz.\n2\tDefeat merrevail and mervyl (total: 14)\030Defeat Ugurzhik\tMerrevail and mervyl can be found at Shakam Moz in Rath Dúath. You should defeat winged folk at Shakam Moz.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many members of Lhaereth's host at Shakam Moz.\n",
[10893]="70053E71\n1\tDestroy perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz\tMerrevail and mervyl perches as well as food sacks can be found at Shakam Moz in Rath Dúath. You should destroy perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz.\n2\tDestroy food sacks (total: 10)\030Destroy perches (total: 8)\tPerches and food sacks belonging to the winged folk can be found at Shakam Moz in Rath Dúath. You should destroy perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroyed many perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz.\n",
[10894]="70053E74\n1\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n2\tClaim the first encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n3\tClaim the second encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n4\tClaim the final encampment for Gondor\tThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.\n5\tCompleted\tClaimed this area for Gondor!\n",
[10895]="7002C38F\n1\tBurn diseased wolf-corpses (total: 6)\tWolf-corpses can be found scattered about the Murderous Pit. You should burn the wolf-corpses to prevent the disease from spreading.\n2\tTalk to Brifard\tBrifard can be found at the camp to the west, just outside of Thinglad. You should return to Brifard and inform him of your discovery.\n",
[10896]="70015010\n1\tDestroy goblin-platforms (total: 3)\tThe goblin-platforms are near the goblin camp of Gazatmur in the Great Delving. Wigfast has asked you to bring down a few of the goblin's archer-platforms with a simple hammer.\n2\tReturn to Wigfast\tWigfast is at his hiding spot outside Gazatmur in the great Delving. You should return to Wigfast and let him know that you have destroyed the goblin archer-platforms as he requested.\n",
[10897]="7006422F\n1\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur and entertain the customers of the Prancing Pony\tBarliman Butterbur can be found at the Prancing Pony, in Bree-town.\n2\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur\tBarliman Butterbur can be found at the Prancing Pony, in Bree-town.\n",
[10898]="70019177\n1\tGather birch-wood (total: 5)\030Gather stone (total: 5)\tThavronwë has asked that you gather stone and wood for him. There is a high concentration of birch east and north of Cerin Amroth, in the grove of Cerin Brethil. Stone can be found to the east, in Gworast on the banks of the Anduin.\n2\tReturn to Thavronwë\030Collect Birch-wood (total: 5)\030Collect Stone (total: 5)\tThavronwë is atop the flet in Cerin Amroth. You should return to Thavronwë and give him the raw materials you fetched for him.\n",
[10899]="70021EEE\n1\tGather wild essences (total: 8)\tThe wild spirits known as elhudan can be found throughout the Mournshaws. Tûm has asked you to gather the essence of the elhudan that haunt the Mournshaws.\n2\tBring the wild essence to Tûm at Gwaed Brun\tTûm is at Gwaed Brun at the heart of the Mournshaws. You should return to Tûm with the essence you have procured.\n",
[10900]="70017591\n1\tTake the fragments to Mirwen in Rivendell\tMirwen is in Elrond's Library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, far to the north of Moria. Winiel has asked you to take the fragments to an Elf named Mirwen.\n",
[10901]="70062DE6\n1\tFind Bedwyr and confront him\tMelona told you the brigand Bedwyr, her latest bounty, should be somewhere to the north-east, not far away.\n2\tTalk to Melona in Sedgemead\tMelona is in Sedgemead, waiting to hear of your encounter with her bounty.\n",
[10902]="7001A494\n1\tTalk to Toly Brockhouse in Buckland\tToly Brockhouse can be found outside the stable near Brandy Hall. Trumric Ragwort asked you to seek a waggon from Toly Brockhouse to help transport all the goods that he and his fellows have collected since arriving in Buckland.\n2\tTalk to Trumric Ragwort in Newbury\tTrumric Ragwort is awaiting your return in Newbury, just inside the gates of Buckland. Toly Brockhouse seemed concerned with events in the Old Forest, but was amenable to lending Trumric Ragwort the waggon for his journey to Adso's camp.\n",
[10903]="7001A9A8\n1\tDefeat Sharkey's Lieutenant at the Southwatch\tSharkey's Lieutenant can be found at his perch, high and far to the south-west, within the Southwatch. Watcher Brittleleaf wants to see the leader of the forces at the Southwatch slain.\n2\tTalk to Watcher Brittleleaf\tWatcher Brittleleaf awaits your return to the east of the northern entrance of the ruins. You hunted down and defeated Sharkey's Lieutenant, but the brigands and half-orcs seemed unaffected by his defeat.\n",
[10904]="70000771\n1\tBring the brigand medallion to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\030Find evidence of the brigands' loyalty\tBrigands have overrun Dogwood's Farm, across the road and north alongside a small stream. Chief Grimbriar awaits your return at the stone house near the cross-roads outside of Bree. Chief Watcher Grimbriar has asked you to investigate the increased brigand activity. He mentioned a small farm across the road and a few paces north he thought was overrun.\n",
[10905]="7005314D\n1\tTalk to Tautila in the Warrens\tTautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen. Tautila has asked for your aid in escaping before Sharkey returns to the warrens of Tûn Melen.\n2\tTalk to Tautila\tTautila can be found just outside the Warrens in the Gladden Fields. You saved Tautila and defeated a half-orc, Garmog, who sought to deceive Sharkey's Men. You should talk to Tautila.\n",
[10906]="7000075A\n1\tBring the letter to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\030Search the brigand-captain's tent\tThe Brigands' Watch sits on a hill north of Adso's camp, and directly west of Grimbriar's Post. Watcher Grimbriar is at his post near the cross-roads of Bree. Grimbriar has instructed you to search the tent of the brigand-captain at the Brigands' Watch to find any correspondence from Sharkey that may divulge information about his plans.\n",
[10907]="70059436\n1\tCollect whetstones (total: 6)\tWhetstones can be found in the Wildwood. You should find and collect whetstones for the League of the Axe.\n2\tSharpen axes (quantity: see journal)\tDull axes can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should sharpen axes with the whetstones you have collected.\n3\tTalk to Mal Knapweed\tMal Knapweed can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Mal Knapweed.\n",
[10908]="700529A0\n1\tDestroy cages to save the animals (total: 10)\tSomehow, the wargs have built cages to hold captive animals, and they must be destroyed.\n",
[10909]="700529A4\n1\tDefeat wargs in Shathur-munzu (total: 12)\030Defeat Brafulug wranglers (total: 6)\tWargs have become a threat to the good folk of the Vales of Anduin, and must be defeated.\n",
[10910]="7005299D\n1\tDefeat Kasak\030Defeat Dúlkoth\tDefeat Kasak and Dúlkoth, the kin of Drokstaz.\n",
[10911]="700529A6\n1\tFree captive sheep from the wargs (total: 8)\tSome sheep have been captured by the wargs of Duskenvale. If you can free the captive sheep, you will have deprived the wargs of a future meal.\n",
[10912]="7000AC56\n1\tDeliver the shattered blades to Soldier Glat\030Collect Shattered Blade (total: 5)\tThe Free Peoples carry weapons from which the blades can be taken and used to craft crossbow bolts. The Free Peoples can be found at any of the locations they control, including the encampment south of Tol Ascarnen. In an effort to better fortify Tol Ascarnen, the War-tyrant has called to the goblins at Grothum and told his soldiers to craft bolts for the goblins to shoot into the tunnel at the mouth of the keep. Glat has left the task of obtaining the blades of the Free Peoples to you.\n",
})
